{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-25T22:00:53.214Z","data":{"text":"Task 9 complete.\n\n**Summary of what I did:**\n\n1. **New `src/core/foundation/traceability-block.ts`** — renders both `AGENTS.md` and `PLANNER.md` blocks with the exact delta text, scoped to `every capability` for `'all'` or the opted-in names joined by `, `. Writes the block directly after the managed block's `<!-- OSQ:END -->` line (or end of file), and removes it symmetrically so a stop-opt-in restores the files byte-for-byte. Exports `checkTraceabilityBlocks` with the three exact doctor messages.\n\n2. **`init.ts`** — one `writeTraceabilityBlocks` call in `scaffoldProject` after `writeRulesBlock`, plus `updatedTraceability` on `InitResult`.\n\n3. **`doctor-managed.ts`** — `checkManagedBlocks` appends traceability problems as their own group, preserving the exact `; run \\`osq init\\`` messages.\n\n4. **`tests/trace-blocks.test.ts`** — covers both delta scenarios, a two-name list, `'all'`, idempotent second init, byte-exact removal, and all three doctor messages through `checkManagedBlocks`.\n\n5. **`README.md`** — new `### Traceability` section (config, table format, helper API and every failure message, tags/forms, `## Scenarios`, `OSQ_CHANGE`, lint findings/modes, report/show lines).\n\n6. **`AGENTS.md`** — `## Layout` gained `trace/` and `src/testing/`; nothing in the managed block changed.\n\n**Verification:** task verify `node --import tsx --test tests/trace-blocks.test.ts` passes (9/9), and the proposal verify `pnpm verify` passes (typechecks, build, full suite, lint).\n\nOne deviation worth flagging: the write call sits after `updatePlannerMd` (still after `writeRulesBlock`) because `PLANNER.md` must exist before the block can land after its managed block."}}
